    "id": 17,
    "num": 17,
    "title": "Meeting",
    "topic": "project meeting place on campus",
    "audioUrl": "/audios/SGD_17_Meeting.mp3",
    "transcript": "Narration: Three students are discussing their project meeting place on campus.\n\nSpeaker1: I think we should meet in a conference room in the university library. We can conveniently borrow books we need right there while we work. It's a quiet space with plenty of resources, and we won't have to carry heavy books around later. Plus, the library has those small study rooms we can book if we need complete privacy.\n\nSpeaker2: I'm not so sure about that idea—the library is always so crowded during this time of day. There will be too many people studying and chatting outside the rooms, and it will be very noisy even inside the conference areas. Last time I tried to study there, I could hardly concentrate with all the distractions. Maybe we should consider someplace else that's actually quiet.\n\nSpeaker3: I have a compromise—we can go to the library first to borrow all the books we need for our research. Then, we can move to a coffee shop to sit down and assign tasks to each other properly. If we run into any issues later or can't meet in person, we can always continue our discussion online. This way we get the resources we need and a comfortable space to talk.\n\nSpeaker1: That's actually a smart plan. Which coffee shop were you thinking about? There are several near campus, but most tend to be quite busy in the afternoons. I remember the one near the south gate has good space, but it's always packed with students. Maybe we should look for someplace less popular?\n\nSpeaker2: I like the idea, but I have to go back home around 4 PM to receive a package that's being delivered. I don't want to miss it since it's something important for the project. I can join you guys after that, though it might make me a little late for the meeting. Would it be okay if I catch up with you both later?\n\nSpeaker3: That should be fine. Just remember to call us when you go out of home so we know when to expect you. We can start without you and fill you in when you arrive. If anything urgent comes up, we can always hop on a quick online call to keep you in the loop.\n\nSpeaker1: Sounds good! Now back to picking a coffee shop—I've been to almost all of them around here, and most do have too many people during this time. What about that new place called \"Honey Cup\"? It's a bit farther from campus, but I heard they have amazing pastries and plenty of seating.\n\nSpeaker2: I've passed by Honey Cup a few times—it does look cozy, and they have those big booths at the back. More importantly, it usually has fewer people compared to chains like Starbucks. Plus, who can say no to sweet treats while working, right?\n\nSpeaker3: Great, then it's settled! We'll meet at the library at 3 PM, get our books, then walk over to Honey Cup to assign tasks and discuss the project outline. Don't forget to call us when you're on your way!",
    "keyPoints": "*Key points:\n\nTopic：project meeting place on campus.\n\n主题：校园内项目会议的地点\n\nSpeaker One (Male)\n\n-Proposal（提议）\n\n1.They should meet in a conference room in the university library.\n\n他们应该在大学图书馆的会议室碰面。\n\n2.They can borrow books there and it's a quiet space with resources.\n\n那里可以借书，是安静且有学习资源的场所。\n\n3.The library has small study rooms to book for privacy.\n\n图书馆有小型研讨室可预订，保障私密性。\n\n-Concern（担忧）\n\n1.Most campus coffee shops are busy in the afternoons.\n\n校园里大多数咖啡店下午都很拥挤。\n\n2.Finding a less popular coffee shop is a major concern.\n\n找到一家不那么热门的咖啡店是主要担忧点。\n\nSpeaker Two (Male)\n\n-Objection to Library（反对图书馆）\n\n1.The library is crowded and noisy.\n\n图书馆又挤又吵。\n\n2.He could hardly concentrate in the library.\n\n他在图书馆里几乎无法集中注意力。\n\n-Time & Preference（时间与偏好）\n\n1.He can join the meeting later.\n\n他可以晚一点参加会议。\n\n2.\"Honey Cup\" is a good coffee shop choice.\n\n“蜜杯” 咖啡店是个不错的选择。\n\nSpeaker Three (Female)\n\n-Compromise Plan（折中方案）\n\n1.Agreed with a compromise of library first then coffee shop.\n\n同意先在图书馆碰面，之后转去咖啡店的折中方案。\n\n2.Borrowing books first then moving to a coffee shop.\n\n先借书，之后转移到咖啡店继续讨论。\n\n3.Meeting at the library at 3 PM then going to \"Honey Cup\".\n\n下午 3 点在图书馆碰面，之后去 “蜜杯” 咖啡店。\n\n-Backup Plan（备用方案）\n\n1.Continuing the discussion online if they can't meet in person.\n\n如果无法线下碰面，就继续在线讨论。\n\n-Coordination（协调）\n\n1.Speaker two can join later and they can start without him.\n\n第二位发言者可以晚到，大家可以先开始讨论。\n\n2.Speaker two should call them when he goes out.\n\n第二位发言者出门时要打电话告知他们。",
    "modelAnswer": "The discussion involves three people talking about their project meeting place on campus.\nThe speaker one first mentioned they should meet in a conference room in the university library.\nAnd then, the speaker has explained that they can borrow books there and it's a quiet space with resources.\nFollowed by that, in the discussion, he mentioned the library has small study rooms to book for privacy.\nFrom him, we know that most campus coffee shops are busy in the afternoons.\nSo basically, according to him, finding a less popular coffee shop is a major concern.\nThe second speaker is mainly about disagreeing with the library and having time constraints.\nFirstly, the speaker emphasized that the library is crowded and noisy.\nHe also mentioned that he could hardly concentrate in the library.\nIn addition, he suggested that he can join the meeting later.\nAs a result, he finally concluded that \"Honey Cup\" is a good coffee shop choice.\nAs for the third speaker, she agreed with a compromise of library first then coffee shop.\nWhat's more, she shared the opinion about borrowing books first then moving to a coffee shop.\nNext, she had faith in continuing the discussion online if they can't meet in person.\nAfter that, she claimed that Speaker2 can join later and they can start without him.\nBesides, she highlighted the point of Speaker2 calling them when he goes out.\nFinally, she accepted the solution of meeting at the library at 3 PM then going to \"Honey Cup\".\nOverall, they focused on the main topic of their project meeting place on campus.",
    "quickNotes": {
      "topic": "project meeting place on campus",
      "s1": [
        "They should meet in a conference room in the university library.",
        "They can borrow books there and it's a quiet space with resources."
      ],
      "s2": [
        "The library is crowded and noisy.",
        "He could hardly concentrate in the library."
      ],
      "s3": [
        "Agreed with a compromise of library first then coffee shop.",
        "Borrowing books first then moving to a coffee shop."
      ]
    }
